SUMMARY:Tina & Her Pony (trio)
DESCRIPTION:Indie Appalachian Folk Band Tina and Her Pony began in Asheville\, North Carolina\, USA in 2010. Shortly thereafter\, they spent two years holed up in the high desert mountain town of Taos\, New Mexico becoming one of the iconic artist colony’s most beloved performing acts. \nThough originally founded as a duo by Tina Collins and Quetzal Jordan\, these days the band is centered around the songwriting of front woman Tina Collins\, a classically trained musician who first toured with her band Over Under Yonder\, a five piece that played songs from Collins’ debut album Journey Onward (2009). Collins composed the songs that appear on Journey Onward as she thru-hiked from Maine to Georgia on the Appalachian Trail. When Over Under Yonder finished touring in 2010\, the band reformed as Tina and Her Pony. Collins’ songwriting incorporates complexities in harmony and arrangement that queer the American folk tradition. Her unique sound draws inspiration from artists such as Gillian Welch\, Sarah Jarosz and Watchhouse. \n  \nFounded in 2005\, Pisgah is known for producing some of the most sought after craft ales in Western North Carolina. Pisgah Brewing Company currently operates the new indoor taproom & deli\, with live music several days a week\, plus an open air outdoor bar in the summer and fall months. Check out our upcoming schedule at pisgahbrewing.com/events
URL:https://livemusicasheville.com/calendar/tina-her-pony-trio/
LOCATION:Pisgah Brewing Company Black Mountain\, 2948 US-70\, Black Mountain\, NC\, 28711
CATEGORIES:Asheville Area,Black Mountain,Live Music
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://livemusicasheville.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/653386313_1405070171647155_3541347435975333516_n-e1774644183729.jpg
GEO:35.6068069;-82.3568213
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Pisgah Brewing Company Black Mountain 2948 US-70 Black Mountain NC 28711;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=2948 US-70:geo:-82.3568213,35.6068069
END:VEVENT
